      "id": 13,
      "options": {
        "content": "## ℹ️ About This Demo Dashboard\n\n**Why do panels show \"No data\"?**\n\nThis is a **template/showcase dashboard** that demonstrates panel type configurations. The queries are examples that would work with typical monitoring data.\n\n**To use this dashboard:**\n\n1. **Replace example queries** with your actual metrics:\n   - `http_requests_total` → your request counter metric\n   - `cpu_usage_percent` → your CPU metric\n   - `up` → your availability metric\n\n2. **Connect your data sources** in each panel's query editor\n\n3. **Adjust time ranges** to match when you have data\n\n**What you can learn:**\n- ✅ Panel type configurations (timeseries, table, barchart, etc.)\n- ✅ Field config (thresholds, colors, units)\n- ✅ Transformations (seriesToRows for tables)\n- ✅ Layout and styling (gridPos, custom HTML)\n- ✅ Visualization options for each panel type\n\n**Next Steps:** Edit any panel to see its configuration and adapt it for your metrics!",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "💡 No Data? That's Normal!",
      "type": "text"
